      },
      "text": "09.11 · Cusco’s Inca Sites and Flight to Lima"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "aafb3dee62679439454d853a9fddb23b554cd726cea29db6f44e5a1b1dde738e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-eab366ae-e542-49a4-8e67-bf54cf3f8a2d",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Explore Cusco with an English-speaking guide, visiting Qorikancha, Q’enqo, Puka Pukara, Tambomachay and Sacsayhuamán. After the tour, transfer to the airport and fly to Lima. On arrival, transfer to your hotel."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:99aeeb8ccaef6c7e",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "aafb3dee62679439454d853a9fddb23b554cd726cea29db6f44e5a1b1dde738e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-eab366ae-e542-49a4-8e67-bf54cf3f8a2d",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Explore Cusco with an English-speaking guide, visiting Qorikancha, Q’enqo, Puka Pukara, Tambomachay and Sacsayhuamán. After the tour, transfer to the airport and fly to Lima. On arrival, transfer to your hotel."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:6e5686392333a3ba",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f808f181e29c32128efa59a2d6be981fda09e3a4c4309d1abbcec96d792dd977",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-eab366ae-e542-49a4-8e67-bf54cf3f8a2d",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Explore Cusco with an English-speaking guide and visit Qorikancha, the Temple of the Sun. The Incas held their main winter solstice ceremony here. Then visit four nearby sites: the temple of Q’enqo, the red fortress of Puka Pukara, Tambomachay, an Inca site devoted to the worship of water, and Sacsayhuamán, a complex of religious structures, fortifications, towers and channels built from enormous stone blocks."
    },
